  "description": "BIXZOZ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C150 H95 Dy5 I20 O25,5(C7 H8). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.517-5.053 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.61-159.86°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C150H95Dy5I20O25·(C7H8). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 5 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
